201
00:08:41,660 --> 00:08:42,680
You can interact with them.

202
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:43,600
You can touch them.

203
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:44,660
You can breathe them.

204
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:49,020
But they are completely invisible if you are only looking at the map on your phone.

205
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:54,880
And Flixian mathematically proves that because any symbol system, whether it's a map, a written

206
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:59,840
word, or a mathematical equation, has a finite, limited description length.

207
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,480
Compared to the infinite complexity of reality.

208
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,060
Exactly.

209
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:07,620
Because of that limitation, these fibers absolutely must exist.

210
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:09,660
Information must be lost.

211
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,260
There is simply no such thing as a perfect, lossless map.

212
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:16,860
Which brings us back to why a trajectory is more real than a static state.

213
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:17,380
Yes.

214
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:23,140
A trajectory, which is movement over time through a space, carries strictly more information

215
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:25,820
than any instantaneous state description ever could.

