424
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:50,320
They go silent because they lack the language of constraints.

425
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:55,340
They can't explain why the rules just changed because they never explicitly mapped the constraints

426
00:18:55,340 --> 00:18:55,940
to begin with.

427
00:18:56,860 --> 00:19:02,400
But Fliction's accessibility geometry, by tracking the constraints themselves rather

428
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:08,020
than the objects, provides the exact mathematical substrate needed to model these boundary cases.

429
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:11,920
I am fascinated by this, but I have to play Dell's advocate for a second.

