00:46:00,580 --> 00:46:11,300
By shifting your focus from arguing about static things to analyzing the geometry of accessibility and constraints, you might just find a trajectory to a solution that you literally couldn't see before.

960
00:46:11,300 --> 00:46:25,420
I couldn't agree more. Knowledge is most valuable when it is applied to our human experience, and mapping the invisible accessibility landscape of your own life, recognizing your own constraints, is an incredibly powerful exercise in empathy and critical thinking.

